cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Concord, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Concord: a governed workflow for AI coding agents"
abstract: "Concord keeps people in control of AI coding agents. A strong model plans each change and checks the result, low-cost models implement it, an independent reviewer checks every change at its risk level, and a small dispatcher enforces tests first and review tiers while recording every verdict with its cause. The dispatcher rejects a run that changed a file outside the phase's declared files, and only on OpenCode is such an edit refused while the run is in progress."
authors:
